      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:ul><html:li><html:strong>allow-import-from-derivation = true</html:strong> — verified this is still required: <html:code>~/ocaml-forester</html:code> uses <html:code>opam-nix</html:code>, which performs IFD during evaluation, and <html:code>~/forest</html:code>'s flake consumes it. Comment in <html:code>configuration.nix</html:code> updated to reflect the real dependency.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>Three zsh plugin systems</html:strong> — the original audit cited a <html:code>syntaxHighlighting</html:code>/<html:code>fast-syntax-highlighting</html:code> conflict, but <html:code>fast-syntax-highlighting</html:code> is no longer in the config. Current setup (zplug for pure + vi-mode, oh-my-zsh for <html:code>git</html:code> aliases, home-manager native options) works without a concrete defect. Not worth churning.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>trusted-users includes stevenschaefer</html:strong> (LOW) — acceptable for single-user Mac.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>Third-party claude-code-nix flake</html:strong> — accepted for now; may self-package later.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>Duplicated Emacs, Agda+Rust overlays, <html:code>.agda/libraries</html:code>, and <html:code>i18n</html:code></html:strong> — cosmetic DRY cleanups, not priority.</html:li></html:ul>
